1
00:00:17,413 --> 00:00:19,749
No wonder the name sounded familiar.

2
00:00:21,084 --> 00:00:22,877
I was Je Moon-jae too.

3
00:00:34,389 --> 00:00:36,099
I said I'm Je Moon-jae!

4
00:01:13,011 --> 00:01:16,139
MOUSETRAP

5
00:01:17,265 --> 00:01:19,601
Ms. Han, let me explain it in person.

6
00:01:19,684 --> 00:01:22,228
You're the only person I can rely on now.

7
00:01:23,396 --> 00:01:26,107
I'll explain everything in person.
Please just hear me out.

8
00:01:26,191 --> 00:01:28,234
Say something already!

9
00:01:28,735 --> 00:01:30,236
Why won't you say anything?

10
00:01:32,822 --> 00:01:33,740
Ms. Han.

11
00:01:45,501 --> 00:01:46,377
See?

12
00:01:46,878 --> 00:01:48,588
I told you he'd call again.

13
00:01:57,347 --> 00:02:00,642
Thank you for the drink.
I'm sorry for showing up unannounced.

14
00:02:02,644 --> 00:02:05,855
Still, we should do this again sometime.

15
00:02:34,384 --> 00:02:35,635
You have a knife.

16
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:40,098
Just kill me already, you bastard!

17
00:02:54,946 --> 00:02:57,031
Come on, pick up.

18
00:03:15,383 --> 00:03:17,051
You can't park here.

19
00:03:17,135 --> 00:03:19,012
It's by the sea. It's dangerous.

20
00:03:19,721 --> 00:03:21,681
Okay, I'll move right away.

21
00:03:21,764 --> 00:03:24,225
Have you been drinking?

22
00:03:25,727 --> 00:03:26,602
No.

23
00:03:31,941 --> 00:03:33,276
Step out for a moment.

24
00:03:33,359 --> 00:03:34,527
-Sorry?
-Sir.

25
00:03:39,741 --> 00:03:41,451
Wanted vehicle. Urgent.

26
00:03:42,368 --> 00:03:43,661
Is this your vehicle?

27
00:03:45,246 --> 00:03:46,581
Please step out.

28
00:03:47,123 --> 00:03:49,375
I don't understand what's going on.

29
00:03:49,459 --> 00:03:51,419
Where the hell is Sun-yong anyway?

30
00:03:57,300 --> 00:04:00,219
What do you mean your name's Moon-jae?

31
00:04:01,637 --> 00:04:03,890
I used to be Je Moon-jae too.

32
00:04:05,308 --> 00:04:06,726
You know I'm an orphan.

33
00:04:08,353 --> 00:04:12,690
The bastard who dragged me into this
even had my adoption records.

34
00:04:14,901 --> 00:04:16,694
Hey, man.

35
00:04:16,778 --> 00:04:19,280
How could you forget your childhood name?

36
00:04:19,781 --> 00:04:21,866
You've been after Je Moon-jae
for a while now.

37
00:04:21,949 --> 00:04:23,368
Come on.

38
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:26,245
Do you still fucking

39
00:04:26,746 --> 00:04:29,082
remember everything clearly
from when you were five?

40
00:04:30,875 --> 00:04:32,210
I've got a lot of names.

41
00:04:34,003 --> 00:04:36,005
I was adopted and returned three times.

42
00:04:36,589 --> 00:04:39,509
I think my first name was Sang-gyu,
Sang-gu, hogu, or something.

43
00:04:39,592 --> 00:04:40,635
Fucking hell.

44
00:04:41,135 --> 00:04:44,222
What was the next one? Hyeon-cheol?

45
00:04:44,305 --> 00:04:46,015
The next one's Park Sun-yong.

46
00:04:47,058 --> 00:04:49,268
But my name was Je Moon-jae
when I was five.

47
00:04:51,062 --> 00:04:52,730
Damn.

48
00:04:53,231 --> 00:04:55,608
No wonder it sounded fucking familiar.

49
00:04:55,691 --> 00:04:57,151
I said get out of the car.

50
00:04:57,652 --> 00:04:59,946
-That's not it.
-I said step out for a moment.

51
00:05:04,534 --> 00:05:06,077
Don't move! Damn it.

52
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:09,539
Get out of the car, you bastard!

53
00:05:09,622 --> 00:05:10,623
Get out!

54
00:05:43,448 --> 00:05:44,490
But…

55
00:05:47,910 --> 00:05:49,495
who are you?

56
00:05:57,253 --> 00:05:58,921
Requesting backup.

57
00:06:00,089 --> 00:06:01,591
Don't move, you bastard.

58
00:06:12,268 --> 00:06:14,187
He said we should rest before we return.

59
00:06:15,104 --> 00:06:16,355
Get some sleep.

60
00:06:38,294 --> 00:06:40,087
Hey, who is it?

61
00:06:42,965 --> 00:06:44,133
Where is the bastard?

62
00:06:45,593 --> 00:06:47,094
He's fine.

63
00:06:47,845 --> 00:06:49,430
That's enough. Bring him out.

64
00:06:49,514 --> 00:06:50,348
Yes, sir.

65
00:07:00,024 --> 00:07:00,858
Hey.

66
00:07:00,942 --> 00:07:01,901
Get in here.

67
00:07:01,984 --> 00:07:03,361
Hey, you bastard. Get in here.

68
00:07:11,619 --> 00:07:12,745
Where's Noja?

69
00:07:14,163 --> 00:07:15,331
I don't know.

70
00:07:16,457 --> 00:07:19,377
Three of our guys died,
you fucking piece of shit!

71
00:07:20,127 --> 00:07:23,172
One of them was expecting a second child,
so he even bought drinks.

72
00:07:23,965 --> 00:07:25,091
You son of a bitch.

73
00:07:25,174 --> 00:07:27,927
Why did our guys have to die
over trash like you?

74
00:07:30,137 --> 00:07:31,389
Tell me where he is.

75
00:07:31,889 --> 00:07:33,182
Noja.

76
00:07:33,683 --> 00:07:35,434
Tell me!

77
00:07:37,728 --> 00:07:38,896
You fucking bastard.

78
00:07:57,582 --> 00:07:59,709
HOW DID IT GO?

79
00:08:00,459 --> 00:08:02,044
PARK SEUNG-GYU

80
00:08:10,928 --> 00:08:13,097
Yeah, I was just about to call you.

81
00:08:13,723 --> 00:08:15,349
I got Noja, that bastard,

82
00:08:15,433 --> 00:08:16,642
and found that old man.

83
00:08:16,726 --> 00:08:22,523
DEOKAM NURSING HOME

84
00:08:28,571 --> 00:08:29,947
Hello.

85
00:08:34,201 --> 00:08:36,704
Apparently, a bunch of cops
already came by and left.

86
00:08:36,787 --> 00:08:38,039
But he has dementia.

87
00:08:38,122 --> 00:08:40,124
Doesn't know his own name.
Remembers nothing.

88
00:08:42,293 --> 00:08:44,754
So there's nothing to be scared of.

89
00:08:45,338 --> 00:08:47,923
That old man, he can't prove anything.

90
00:08:49,175 --> 00:08:50,468
So what do we do now?

91
00:08:51,135 --> 00:08:52,386
How do I get my money?

92
00:08:54,930 --> 00:08:57,433
Fuck. You're right.

93
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,312
I didn't even think about that.

94
00:09:03,522 --> 00:09:04,482
Okay.

95
00:09:06,442 --> 00:09:07,735
Got it. Okay.

96
00:09:43,312 --> 00:09:45,981
Why the fuck is he asking me
to send this shit?

97
00:09:46,065 --> 00:09:48,943
Hey, call the guy at the nursing home.
We've missed something.

98
00:10:18,013 --> 00:10:19,807
Please call that detective.

99
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:22,601
Then I'll explain everything.

100
00:10:51,964 --> 00:10:53,215
Where are you going?

101
00:10:53,966 --> 00:10:54,884
The nursing home.

102
00:11:06,729 --> 00:11:07,980
WRITER JE MOON-JAE

103
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:11,901
-Yep.
-Hello, detective. It's Je Moon-jae.

104
00:11:12,485 --> 00:11:14,320
Oh, I know.

105
00:11:14,403 --> 00:11:15,654
But what's this about?

106
00:11:15,738 --> 00:11:17,281
I heard you found my uncle.

107
00:11:18,741 --> 00:11:19,784
Yep.

108
00:11:19,867 --> 00:11:21,786
Then that makes things simpler.

109
00:11:22,369 --> 00:11:25,247
One simple DNA test
will tell you who the real one is.

110
00:11:25,331 --> 00:11:28,250
I just have a feeling you suspect me.

111
00:11:30,169 --> 00:11:31,712
I was thinking the same thing.

112
00:11:32,296 --> 00:11:34,590
I'm actually on my way
to the nursing home.

113
00:11:35,299 --> 00:11:38,469
Are you sure
you're okay with the DNA test?

114
00:11:38,552 --> 00:11:40,888
Of course. Where's my uncle?

115
00:11:40,971 --> 00:11:42,389
I'll head over right now.

116
00:11:42,473 --> 00:11:44,099
I guess you can do that.

117
00:11:44,183 --> 00:11:48,646
First, I'll collect your uncle's hair
and a buccal swab, and…

118
00:11:51,106 --> 00:11:52,316
What the hell?

119
00:11:53,818 --> 00:11:55,486
For fuck's sake.

120
00:11:58,781 --> 00:12:00,366
The patient inhaled a lot of smoke.

121
00:12:11,836 --> 00:12:13,337
For fuck's sake, seriously!

122
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:14,964
Excuse me!

123
00:12:15,047 --> 00:12:17,466
Excuse me. That old man. The elderly man.

124
00:12:17,550 --> 00:12:19,385
He should be nearby. Everyone's out.

125
00:12:19,468 --> 00:12:20,719
-Really?
-It's so hectic.

126
00:12:20,803 --> 00:12:23,681
He should be over there.
He was in the same room as them.

127
00:12:23,764 --> 00:12:24,932
-There?
-Yes.

128
00:12:25,015 --> 00:12:25,933
Okay.

129
00:12:52,459 --> 00:12:56,463
Why are you trembling?
You seemed fine burying your friend there.

130
00:13:02,595 --> 00:13:03,637
What

131
00:13:04,138 --> 00:13:05,556
did I do wrong?

132
00:13:06,181 --> 00:13:07,099
Huh?

133
00:13:07,975 --> 00:13:09,935
If I did something wrong,

134
00:13:11,854 --> 00:13:12,980
I'm sorry.

135
00:13:14,481 --> 00:13:15,733
Really.

136
00:13:16,609 --> 00:13:18,110
I'm really sorry!

137
00:13:18,193 --> 00:13:19,945
Fuck.

138
00:13:20,029 --> 00:13:22,323
Did you even know that I liked you?

139
00:13:23,282 --> 00:13:24,992
I was obsessed with you.

140
00:13:25,075 --> 00:13:28,037
I did everything you told me to do
to fucking impress you.

141
00:13:28,537 --> 00:13:32,416
I did all your dirty work,
and you don't even fucking know who I am.

142
00:13:32,499 --> 00:13:36,003
To someone as mighty as you,
I must've been fucking nobody.

143
00:13:36,086 --> 00:13:39,506
And the mighty man got scammed
and lost fucking everything.

144
00:13:41,508 --> 00:13:42,718
Was that money yours?

145
00:13:43,677 --> 00:13:44,678
Did you make it?

146
00:13:45,179 --> 00:13:47,014
I made it, you son of a bitch.

147
00:13:48,599 --> 00:13:49,558
I'm sorry.

148
00:13:52,353 --> 00:13:53,979
I'm sorry!

149
00:13:54,563 --> 00:13:55,648
I'm sorry!

150
00:13:56,231 --> 00:13:57,066
I'm sorry.

151
00:13:57,149 --> 00:13:59,026
You didn't even know I gave you work

152
00:13:59,109 --> 00:14:01,111
and helped you
when you were broke, did you?

153
00:14:02,112 --> 00:14:05,324
Fuck, you did a hell of a lot of bad shit.
Ten times more than me.

154
00:14:05,991 --> 00:14:07,493
Ten times? Definitely more. Fuck.

155
00:14:07,576 --> 00:14:09,703
Acting all high and mighty,
burying people there.

156
00:14:09,787 --> 00:14:11,497
Did it make you feel like a god?

157
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:12,498
No.

158
00:14:12,581 --> 00:14:14,291
Not at all.

159
00:14:16,460 --> 00:14:20,089
You're not the only one who's gonna die.
So don't be too upset.

160
00:14:40,359 --> 00:14:43,570
I'll bury every fucking bastard
who knows about my past

161
00:14:43,654 --> 00:14:44,822
and leave this country.

162
00:14:45,823 --> 00:14:47,241
Everyone. Even that asshole.

163
00:14:48,909 --> 00:14:50,202
Gotta start a new game.

164
00:14:53,205 --> 00:14:55,499
What if I beg for forgiveness?

165
00:14:56,834 --> 00:14:58,085
Will you spare me?

166
00:15:11,932 --> 00:15:12,933
Go ahead, then.

167
00:15:19,106 --> 00:15:20,899
I'm sorry.

168
00:15:22,234 --> 00:15:23,444
I was wrong.

169
00:15:23,944 --> 00:15:25,070
Please spare me.

170
00:15:26,030 --> 00:15:27,448
Never again!

171
00:15:27,948 --> 00:15:29,533
You'll never see me again!

172
00:15:30,367 --> 00:15:31,827
Just let me live!

173
00:15:32,327 --> 00:15:34,663
Please.

174
00:15:50,679 --> 00:15:52,222
-Sir.
-Good night, sir!

175
00:16:04,109 --> 00:16:05,611
Treat yourself to something nice.

176
00:16:10,032 --> 00:16:11,492
Thank you, sir!

177
00:16:13,202 --> 00:16:14,453
Thank you, sir!

178
00:16:20,959 --> 00:16:22,294
Do you remember?

179
00:16:23,670 --> 00:16:25,339
That time you gave me money.

180
00:16:26,215 --> 00:16:29,384
I was so fucking scared
'cause I thought I was gonna die.

181
00:16:29,927 --> 00:16:32,096
There was a time I wanted to be like you.

182
00:16:36,809 --> 00:16:38,143
But I guess I can't anymore.

183
00:16:42,064 --> 00:16:43,482
I'm sorry, but it's too late.

184
00:16:44,733 --> 00:16:45,859
No!

185
00:16:46,443 --> 00:16:47,528
Please!

186
00:16:48,153 --> 00:16:49,321
Spare me!

187
00:16:50,697 --> 00:16:51,907
No!

188
00:16:53,951 --> 00:16:56,036
No! Just spare my life!

189
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,412
Here's your money back.

190
00:16:59,123 --> 00:16:59,998
Bury him.

191
00:17:19,351 --> 00:17:20,519
Aren't you gonna sleep?

192
00:17:22,729 --> 00:17:24,022
I'm thinking.

193
00:17:27,109 --> 00:17:28,402
About what?

194
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:32,030
The dog I had when I was a kid.

195
00:17:33,115 --> 00:17:36,743
We kept it tied up in the yard
to guard the house.

196
00:17:37,244 --> 00:17:40,581
It guarded the house its whole life
until it died of old age.

197
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:42,916
But until it died,

198
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:46,128
it never saw the world beyond that leash.

199
00:17:46,628 --> 00:17:49,339
The length of that leash

200
00:17:49,423 --> 00:17:51,341
was its whole world.

201
00:17:53,719 --> 00:17:55,888
It must've been dying to get out of there.

202
00:17:59,308 --> 00:18:02,686
I don't remember the dog's name,
but as for the leash…

203
00:18:03,187 --> 00:18:05,480
I even remember the color of that leash.

204
00:18:06,481 --> 00:18:11,820
Maybe it's not that I remember the dog,
but that I remember the leash.

205
00:18:13,030 --> 00:18:14,573
Now that I think of it,

206
00:18:14,656 --> 00:18:17,242
in a way,
that leash was the mark of the dog.

207
00:18:20,621 --> 00:18:24,082
Come to think of it, I'm the same too.
Hey, here. Do you see it?

208
00:18:25,334 --> 00:18:26,710
The leash.

209
00:18:27,628 --> 00:18:29,046
There's nothing there.

210
00:18:34,134 --> 00:18:36,637
Everyone has memories they want to erase.

211
00:18:37,262 --> 00:18:38,513
But this leash

212
00:18:39,014 --> 00:18:42,809
is woven from the memories
you want to erase.

213
00:18:42,893 --> 00:18:46,063
Right when you think it's gone,
it grabs you by the throat.

214
00:18:47,689 --> 00:18:49,149
In the end,

215
00:18:50,567 --> 00:18:51,985
people die by that leash.

216
00:18:54,821 --> 00:18:57,783
Hey, didn't you say
your memories were fading?

217
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:00,911
Don't forget about that leash, you punk,

218
00:19:01,411 --> 00:19:02,829
or you'll…

219
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:07,501
never be able to prove who you are.

220
00:19:31,733 --> 00:19:33,110
Je Moon-jae.

221
00:19:33,944 --> 00:19:37,739
It's not even a good name.
Why the hell are you fighting over it?

222
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:40,284
The fake one kills someone,

223
00:19:40,367 --> 00:19:43,078
frames the other,
and pretends to be the real one?

224
00:19:44,955 --> 00:19:47,165
Fuck, who's the real one?
And who's the fake?

225
00:19:47,666 --> 00:19:48,500
Huh?

226
00:19:48,583 --> 00:19:50,002
You wanted to see me.

227
00:19:52,879 --> 00:19:53,839
Please help me.

228
00:19:55,215 --> 00:19:56,049
I've got

229
00:19:56,550 --> 00:19:58,635
no one but you.

230
00:19:59,261 --> 00:20:00,721
What about Noja?

231
00:20:06,184 --> 00:20:07,144
I don't know.

232
00:20:09,104 --> 00:20:10,314
We lost touch.

233
00:20:15,527 --> 00:20:16,945
There he is.

234
00:20:45,932 --> 00:20:46,808
This…

235
00:20:49,353 --> 00:20:50,270
They sent this to you.

236
00:20:52,564 --> 00:20:53,857
He died?

237
00:20:57,527 --> 00:21:01,365
You won't even find the body.
That's the cleanest way.

238
00:21:12,167 --> 00:21:14,461
You found your uncle.
Why did you just leave?

239
00:21:17,172 --> 00:21:19,925
Why did you just leave?
You bastard. Damn it.

240
00:21:23,512 --> 00:21:24,721
He remembered nothing.

241
00:21:27,182 --> 00:21:28,183
There was no point.

242
00:21:28,683 --> 00:21:30,018
DNA.

243
00:21:33,814 --> 00:21:36,316
Hey. What's up with your face?

244
00:21:37,734 --> 00:21:39,736
I'm helping you right now.

245
00:21:40,904 --> 00:21:42,948
You should be happy
if you're the real one.

246
00:21:46,993 --> 00:21:47,869
Can it…

247
00:21:47,953 --> 00:21:48,995
Can it be this easy?

248
00:21:53,917 --> 00:21:55,585
After you came by and left…

249
00:21:57,546 --> 00:21:59,172
your uncle disappeared.

250
00:21:59,256 --> 00:22:02,801
Someone burned down the nursing home
and took it all, even his toothbrush.

251
00:22:02,884 --> 00:22:04,386
In case he left DNA behind.

252
00:22:14,271 --> 00:22:15,439
I knew it.

253
00:22:17,441 --> 00:22:19,276
It can't be this easy.

254
00:22:21,820 --> 00:22:24,114
That's how it's always been so far.

255
00:22:26,741 --> 00:22:30,829
That bastard knows everything about me.
He knows me better than I do.

256
00:22:30,912 --> 00:22:32,122
I see.

257
00:22:33,373 --> 00:22:35,208
So you don't know anything about this?

258
00:22:35,292 --> 00:22:38,003
I was caught
right after I left the nursing home.

259
00:22:39,254 --> 00:22:40,505
I couldn't have moved him.

260
00:22:40,589 --> 00:22:42,966
Maybe you've got some bastard helping you.

261
00:22:49,389 --> 00:22:50,348
I did.

262
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:57,522
They're tracking his movements on CCTV.

263
00:22:57,606 --> 00:22:58,773
Your uncle.

264
00:22:58,857 --> 00:23:00,859
You don't even have an alibi.

265
00:23:01,359 --> 00:23:02,903
So if we can't find him,

266
00:23:03,820 --> 00:23:05,614
you're the fake one.

267
00:23:06,364 --> 00:23:08,116
That's why I asked to see you.

268
00:23:08,617 --> 00:23:10,827
I'll tell you everything
that's happened so far.

269
00:23:10,911 --> 00:23:12,579
Who he is,

270
00:23:14,372 --> 00:23:15,707
what happened…

271
00:23:18,168 --> 00:23:19,586
and how it ended up like this.

272
00:23:22,964 --> 00:23:23,965
Hey, guys. Listen up.

273
00:23:24,049 --> 00:23:27,385
I first met him
at an intercollegiate literature club.

274
00:23:27,469 --> 00:23:31,056
We got a new member today.
What? Is he handsome?

275
00:23:31,932 --> 00:23:32,933
Introduce yourself.

276
00:23:35,101 --> 00:23:38,063
Hello, I'm the new club member,

277
00:23:38,146 --> 00:23:39,856
Seo Yu-min.

278
00:23:40,357 --> 00:23:41,816
It's very nice to meet you all.

279
00:23:43,401 --> 00:23:44,819
Welcome.

280
00:23:46,488 --> 00:23:48,031
His first impression wasn't good.

281
00:23:49,282 --> 00:23:50,200
How should I put it?

282
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:54,746
He had a ravenous look in his eyes,
like he hadn't eaten in days.

283
00:23:56,164 --> 00:24:00,043
The kind of look that makes you think
he'd devour anything.

284
00:24:03,088 --> 00:24:05,298
THE RAT THAT ATE FINGERNAILS

285
00:24:15,016 --> 00:24:16,851
Moon-jae, did you write this?

286
00:24:17,352 --> 00:24:19,020
Why? You think it's good?

287
00:24:19,854 --> 00:24:20,689
It's amazing.

288
00:24:24,442 --> 00:24:25,402
I'm jealous.

289
00:24:25,902 --> 00:24:27,696
I wish I could write like you.

290
00:24:27,779 --> 00:24:28,613
Man.

291
00:24:28,697 --> 00:24:31,199
But I'm too lazy.

292
00:24:31,283 --> 00:24:34,536
I still have this much to write,
but I'm getting nowhere.

293
00:24:52,387 --> 00:24:55,932
Actually, there's someone who inspires me.

294
00:24:56,016 --> 00:24:57,017
Who is it?

295
00:25:05,734 --> 00:25:07,360
You're gonna wear it out.

296
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:10,405
The two of us grew close quickly.

297
00:25:10,488 --> 00:25:12,198
This is how people end up alcoholics…

298
00:25:12,282 --> 00:25:14,951
It was because of Min-yeong.

299
00:25:15,619 --> 00:25:16,453
Bathroom.

300
00:25:16,536 --> 00:25:17,370
We both…

301
00:25:17,454 --> 00:25:18,496
Get me one more.

302
00:25:18,580 --> 00:25:20,373
…liked Min-yeong.

303
00:25:22,208 --> 00:25:24,044
She can really hold her liquor.

304
00:25:28,632 --> 00:25:29,966
What is it?

305
00:25:33,845 --> 00:25:34,679
Moon-jae.

306
00:25:37,432 --> 00:25:38,892
What's the deal with you two?

307
00:25:38,975 --> 00:25:42,020
What do you mean?
We just go to the same school.

308
00:25:42,854 --> 00:25:44,064
You're sure, right?

309
00:25:47,150 --> 00:25:50,945
Whether I'm sure or not,
talking about this is meaningless.

310
00:25:56,159 --> 00:25:57,494
Why is it meaningless?

311
00:25:57,577 --> 00:25:59,913
Min-yeong is way out of our league.

312
00:25:59,996 --> 00:26:03,333
Her standards are super high.
We're not even close.

313
00:26:04,793 --> 00:26:06,461
She's definitely out of your league.

314
00:26:09,964 --> 00:26:11,216
But not mine.

315
00:26:29,275 --> 00:26:30,568
That summer,

316
00:26:31,361 --> 00:26:33,488
the three of us went on a trip together.

317
00:26:57,846 --> 00:27:00,932
But something happened there.

318
00:28:24,516 --> 00:28:25,600
Min-yeong.

319
00:28:26,142 --> 00:28:28,102
I've got something to tell you.
Let's talk.

320
00:28:29,646 --> 00:28:31,147
You're drunk. Talk tomorrow.

321
00:28:31,231 --> 00:28:33,316
Let go! I just wanna talk to her.

322
00:28:34,818 --> 00:28:36,528
You said you two weren't a thing.

323
00:28:45,954 --> 00:28:47,413
We're dating.

324
00:28:49,082 --> 00:28:52,961
We kept it a secret at the club
because he said he'd feel uncomfortable.

325
00:29:00,385 --> 00:29:01,386
Since when?

326
00:29:02,470 --> 00:29:03,888
Before you asked me.

327
00:29:08,726 --> 00:29:11,646
You shouldn't toy with people.

328
00:29:11,729 --> 00:29:13,606
Don't you fucking think so?

329
00:29:30,832 --> 00:29:31,958
You are just

330
00:29:32,458 --> 00:29:33,751
jealous of me.

331
00:29:34,377 --> 00:29:37,714
You're dying of jealousy
because you want to be me.

332
00:29:37,797 --> 00:29:38,631
Aren't you?

333
00:29:38,715 --> 00:29:41,050
Shut up, you son of a bitch!

334
00:29:57,567 --> 00:30:00,612
That was the last time I ever saw him.

335
00:30:01,237 --> 00:30:03,031
I hadn't seen him since that day.

336
00:30:11,873 --> 00:30:14,500
Until he came back with my face.

337
00:30:14,584 --> 00:30:17,211
You're saying he did all this
just for that?

338
00:30:17,295 --> 00:30:19,088
I don't understand either.

339
00:30:19,172 --> 00:30:20,798
Is this really worth all this?

340
00:30:26,554 --> 00:30:30,058
He went ballistic,
like someone took what was his.

341
00:30:32,268 --> 00:30:36,147
Does it make any sense that he changed
his face to yours and killed that girl

342
00:30:36,230 --> 00:30:37,565
after all this time?

343
00:30:38,358 --> 00:30:40,652
There must be more to it, you bastard.

344
00:30:42,862 --> 00:30:43,863
There is.

345
00:30:44,822 --> 00:30:46,491
Something I didn't know about.

346
00:30:48,284 --> 00:30:49,869
I heard about this later,

347
00:30:50,620 --> 00:30:53,998
but that bastard
wasn't even a university student.

348
00:30:54,749 --> 00:30:56,834
He was pretending to be one
from the start.

349
00:30:57,835 --> 00:30:58,836
Creepy, isn't it?

350
00:30:59,337 --> 00:31:01,255
What happened between you and that girl?

351
00:31:03,675 --> 00:31:04,509
Well,

352
00:31:05,760 --> 00:31:06,928
it just fizzled out.

353
00:31:08,262 --> 00:31:11,391
I heard she met someone later
and lived with him.

354
00:31:13,559 --> 00:31:15,228
We shouldn't have gone on that trip.

355
00:31:15,311 --> 00:31:17,772
That trip's what caused all this mess.

356
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:25,738
Tell me about your parents.

357
00:31:27,991 --> 00:31:30,118
Prove that you're the real one.

358
00:31:30,201 --> 00:31:32,245
Something the fake one wouldn't know.

359
00:31:44,340 --> 00:31:45,341
My mom

360
00:31:46,384 --> 00:31:48,720
had some mental issues.

361
00:31:50,054 --> 00:31:51,973
I don't know why,

362
00:31:52,473 --> 00:31:56,477
but ever since I was born,
our home was never like other families'.

363
00:32:57,497 --> 00:32:59,707
My father said I took after my mom.

364
00:33:00,208 --> 00:33:02,752
Maybe that's why I inherited
her illness too.

365
00:33:06,631 --> 00:33:09,175
After that,
I could feel myself losing my mind.

366
00:33:09,759 --> 00:33:11,594
I couldn't live without my meds.

367
00:33:11,677 --> 00:33:13,054
I'm still like that now.

368
00:33:14,305 --> 00:33:17,558
Maybe it's the meds,
but my old memories are fading.

369
00:33:18,810 --> 00:33:21,395
Once I completely forget who I am,

370
00:33:22,480 --> 00:33:24,273
he will become the real one, right?

371
00:33:25,233 --> 00:33:26,609
The vanity in the bedroom.

372
00:33:28,069 --> 00:33:29,987
What did it look like?

373
00:33:33,574 --> 00:33:34,450
It was just…

374
00:33:36,661 --> 00:33:38,204
a regular vanity.

375
00:33:39,747 --> 00:33:40,581
Black.

376
00:33:43,251 --> 00:33:44,335
A black one.

377
00:33:55,263 --> 00:33:56,722
With no patterns.

378
00:33:57,348 --> 00:33:59,851
Not even shiny. Just black.

379
00:34:03,604 --> 00:34:04,522
A square-shaped one.

380
00:34:05,106 --> 00:34:06,149
A rectangle.

381
00:34:07,316 --> 00:34:08,609
How did you know?

382
00:34:10,153 --> 00:34:12,196
We had one like that at home too.

383
00:34:15,825 --> 00:34:17,827
Now I fucking get it.

384
00:34:20,163 --> 00:34:23,040
My role was to put you in jail.

385
00:34:31,883 --> 00:34:34,552
For one, you don't have much time.
And no alibi either.

386
00:34:34,635 --> 00:34:37,388
Everything you have
is evidence against you.

387
00:34:37,471 --> 00:34:40,266
If you get indicted like this,
you're done.

388
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:44,854
If you have anything more to add,
tell me now.

389
00:34:44,937 --> 00:34:47,315
Anything that proves you're the real one.

390
00:34:48,149 --> 00:34:48,983
All of it.

391
00:35:32,902 --> 00:35:36,322
Yes, that property damage case.
The one with the smashed car.

392
00:35:36,405 --> 00:35:39,492
CONSTRUCTION EQUIPMENT PARTS DEALER

393
00:35:39,575 --> 00:35:41,244
Sir, have a good one.

394
00:35:41,994 --> 00:35:44,497
-So you didn't see anything?
-No, I didn't.

395
00:35:44,580 --> 00:35:45,539
Thank you.

396
00:35:53,005 --> 00:35:56,801
I mean, why are we here looking for CCTVs?

397
00:35:56,884 --> 00:35:59,262
How did this become our case?

398
00:35:59,345 --> 00:36:01,555
The one who knows
is at the police station.

399
00:36:02,139 --> 00:36:05,268
I mean, why's he at another station?

400
00:36:05,351 --> 00:36:07,019
Major Crimes called him.

401
00:36:07,895 --> 00:36:09,605
Seriously.

402
00:36:10,606 --> 00:36:11,524
Hello?

403
00:36:13,401 --> 00:36:14,902
What? Why?

404
00:36:16,904 --> 00:36:17,738
What? Well…

405
00:36:19,365 --> 00:36:20,700
Find anything?

406
00:36:20,783 --> 00:36:21,993
Nothing, of course.

407
00:36:22,076 --> 00:36:23,703
I mean, you have to tell me why…

408
00:36:25,204 --> 00:36:27,707
Who is it? Is it Sun-yong?

409
00:36:27,790 --> 00:36:29,834
-Let me talk to that bastard.
-He hung up.

410
00:36:29,917 --> 00:36:31,210
-What?
-Wait, so…

411
00:36:31,294 --> 00:36:32,628
What did the captain say?

412
00:36:33,838 --> 00:36:35,589
He said to leave Chang-u here.

413
00:36:35,673 --> 00:36:38,301
-He wants the rest of us at the station.
-Me?

414
00:36:39,010 --> 00:36:39,885
Why?

415
00:36:40,720 --> 00:36:43,431
He said he'll tell us when we're there.

416
00:36:43,514 --> 00:36:44,849
That damn bastard.

417
00:36:50,604 --> 00:36:54,692
INTERROGATION ROOM 1

418
00:36:56,068 --> 00:36:57,236
Let's take a break.

419
00:36:57,903 --> 00:36:59,864
We should have him change clothes too.

420
00:37:00,489 --> 00:37:01,574
Let's call for backup.

421
00:37:01,657 --> 00:37:04,535
We have to find Noja's body
or something to close this case.

422
00:37:04,618 --> 00:37:06,787
Seung-gyu and his men are probably nearby.

423
00:37:06,871 --> 00:37:10,082
If we go back to Seoul now,
we won't get anything out of this.

424
00:37:19,592 --> 00:37:23,304
I mean, but why did he ask for you? Huh?

425
00:37:23,387 --> 00:37:25,264
He didn't even say anything useful.

426
00:37:25,348 --> 00:37:26,891
I guess I make people comfortable.

427
00:37:26,974 --> 00:37:28,934
Unlike detectives who beat people.

428
00:37:30,603 --> 00:37:31,771
Maybe that wasn't funny.

429
00:37:32,855 --> 00:37:36,734
You know how our job is.
You get close chasing people around.

430
00:37:36,817 --> 00:37:40,196
He started falling apart
after finding out Noja was dead.

431
00:37:40,279 --> 00:37:43,908
He's slowly starting to talk,
so I'll try to dig deeper.

432
00:37:43,991 --> 00:37:45,326
Go grab lunch.

433
00:37:45,409 --> 00:37:47,453
Just order us two bowls of gukbap.

434
00:37:51,082 --> 00:37:52,208
Let's just go eat.

435
00:37:54,877 --> 00:37:55,711
Let's go.

436
00:37:57,963 --> 00:37:59,840
All right, enjoy your lunch!

437
00:38:21,987 --> 00:38:22,822
Where's my uncle?

438
00:38:24,115 --> 00:38:25,074
Come with me.

439
00:38:43,342 --> 00:38:49,723
INTERROGATION ROOM 2

440
00:38:58,065 --> 00:38:59,024
Where's my uncle?

441
00:39:00,776 --> 00:39:03,654
You didn't even remember him.
Desperate to see him now?

442
00:39:04,905 --> 00:39:08,576
I guess people really are drawn
to the same blood.

443
00:39:09,285 --> 00:39:11,954
The CSI team's coming to take your DNA.

444
00:39:12,037 --> 00:39:14,123
So sit down and wait a bit.

445
00:39:14,707 --> 00:39:16,959
Should I get you something to drink?

446
00:39:22,590 --> 00:39:25,134
Then wait here for a moment.

447
00:39:57,166 --> 00:39:59,793
"Just smuggle him out for now"?
What's going on here?

448
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:03,923
Sir, the whole team's necks
are on the line.

449
00:40:04,006 --> 00:40:06,050
You might even lose your pension.

450
00:40:07,218 --> 00:40:08,552
To hell with it!

451
00:40:09,053 --> 00:40:09,887
Let's just do it.

452
00:40:10,387 --> 00:40:11,388
-Right on.
-Yeah.

453
00:40:12,681 --> 00:40:15,976
Hey, you heard that, right?
We're all risking our necks for this.

454
00:40:16,060 --> 00:40:18,771
-Hurry up, punk.
-Got it? Just follow us quietly.

455
00:40:34,662 --> 00:40:36,664
HAN CHANG-U:
FOUND THE SUSPECT VEHICLE.

456
00:40:36,747 --> 00:40:39,208
TRACED ITS MOVEMENTS.
WHERE IS EVERYONE ANYWAY?

457
00:40:39,959 --> 00:40:41,293
Sir!

458
00:40:41,377 --> 00:40:42,461
Sir, over here.

459
00:40:44,171 --> 00:40:45,172
Here.

460
00:40:47,049 --> 00:40:48,217
Go in. Here.

461
00:40:55,641 --> 00:40:56,559
Yes, here.

462
00:40:58,310 --> 00:40:59,979
You haven't eaten, right?

463
00:41:00,062 --> 00:41:02,356
Well, I felt bad eating by myself.

464
00:41:03,399 --> 00:41:04,984
Let's eat together, all right?

465
00:41:07,194 --> 00:41:08,153
Sir, how much is it?

466
00:41:16,120 --> 00:41:18,038
Wait. I'm not sure I have any coins.

467
00:41:20,958 --> 00:41:22,418
You wanted coffee, right?

468
00:41:22,501 --> 00:41:23,544
Yes.

469
00:41:26,589 --> 00:41:27,423
Oh man.

470
00:41:37,516 --> 00:41:38,350
Hey, you bastard.

471
00:41:39,935 --> 00:41:43,522
He traced the uncle's movements.
We have to find him first.

472
00:41:43,606 --> 00:41:44,857
Hurry up and go.

473
00:41:44,940 --> 00:41:46,400
Hey, you bastard.

474
00:41:46,483 --> 00:41:47,818
Oh, and

475
00:41:47,901 --> 00:41:50,029
I found out
who the woman in the river was.

476
00:41:50,112 --> 00:41:52,114
I'll join you
after checking one more thing.

477
00:41:52,197 --> 00:41:53,282
Go as fast as you can.

478
00:41:53,365 --> 00:41:54,199
Check what?

479
00:41:54,283 --> 00:41:56,869
The evidence that the bastard
is the real one.

480
00:42:00,581 --> 00:42:01,457
What did he say?

481
00:42:03,125 --> 00:42:04,501
No fucking idea.

482
00:42:05,919 --> 00:42:07,379
He said this one's the real one.

483
00:42:23,062 --> 00:42:24,188
It wasn't bad, right?

484
00:42:24,271 --> 00:42:26,398
I actually liked the other place better.

485
00:42:30,736 --> 00:42:31,862
I'm so tired.

486
00:42:39,370 --> 00:42:40,871
You should see this, sir.

487
00:42:45,042 --> 00:42:46,168
What the hell?

488
00:42:46,251 --> 00:42:48,462
Why did he change the interrogation room?

489
00:43:13,070 --> 00:43:14,113
He said he lost him.

490
00:43:14,613 --> 00:43:17,032
He lost an old man
who was barely even alive?

491
00:43:17,866 --> 00:43:20,244
Goddamn it. Fucking bastards.

492
00:43:22,871 --> 00:43:24,039
Which mountain is that?

493
00:43:25,416 --> 00:43:26,250
What do we do?

494
00:43:26,333 --> 00:43:29,420
What do you think? Turn the car around.
You fucking dumbasses!

495
00:43:30,421 --> 00:43:31,255
Fuck.

496
00:43:47,813 --> 00:43:49,314
PARK SEUNG-GYU

497
00:43:58,824 --> 00:43:59,992
Hey, it's me.

498
00:44:00,993 --> 00:44:02,077
He said he lost him.

499
00:44:02,703 --> 00:44:05,372
I'll take care of it. Don't worry.

500
00:44:08,333 --> 00:44:09,835
Fucking idiots.

501
00:44:13,797 --> 00:44:16,800
Hey! That bastard's looking at a phone!

502
00:44:16,884 --> 00:44:18,385
Where did he get it? Hey!

503
00:44:24,308 --> 00:44:25,225
Who are you?

504
00:44:27,936 --> 00:44:28,771
Me?

505
00:44:31,231 --> 00:44:33,275
I'm Je Moon-jae.

506
00:44:34,151 --> 00:44:36,904
Je Moon-jae, the complainant and victim!

507
00:44:49,833 --> 00:44:50,667
Isn't that it?

508
00:44:50,751 --> 00:44:52,878
Yeah, that's it. 1917.

509
00:44:52,961 --> 00:44:55,547
Man, how are we supposed to find him here?

510
00:44:55,631 --> 00:44:58,091
Even the whole Mobile Police Unit
would take a month.

511
00:44:58,175 --> 00:45:00,427
We can't even use drones.
The forest's too dense.

512
00:45:02,346 --> 00:45:06,225
If he went up some remote mountain,
he'd have left traces unless he's a ghost.

513
00:45:06,308 --> 00:45:08,644
Quit whining and follow me, punk.
Time is precious.

514
00:45:09,311 --> 00:45:10,562
-Get your gear.
-Okay.

515
00:45:12,648 --> 00:45:13,941
What about him?

516
00:45:16,902 --> 00:45:19,613
Hey, cuff him to the steering wheel.

517
00:45:19,696 --> 00:45:22,032
Oh, I'll come with you and help.

518
00:45:24,701 --> 00:45:26,829
My uncle is the only evidence.

519
00:45:50,060 --> 00:45:52,771
I'm with the police.
I'd like to check some school records.

520
00:45:57,776 --> 00:45:58,777
He's not here.

521
00:45:58,861 --> 00:46:00,112
STUDENT RECORD
SO MIN-YEONG

522
00:46:00,195 --> 00:46:01,864
What are you talking about? No way.

523
00:46:01,947 --> 00:46:04,491
We never had a student by that name.

524
00:46:04,575 --> 00:46:06,326
Could it have been another school?

525
00:46:07,035 --> 00:46:08,704
No. It's definitely this school.

526
00:46:08,787 --> 00:46:11,081
Please check again.

527
00:46:13,458 --> 00:46:16,670
The student records from the '70s on
have all been computerized.

528
00:46:16,753 --> 00:46:18,964
He wouldn't be from the '60s, right?

529
00:46:19,047 --> 00:46:23,343
Even students who dropped out are in here.
If he's not here, he never attended.

530
00:46:26,889 --> 00:46:28,181
Seo Yu-min.

531
00:46:30,017 --> 00:46:32,686
Can you try searching Seo Yu-min?

532
00:46:32,769 --> 00:46:34,021
Seo Yu-min?

533
00:46:35,314 --> 00:46:38,483
Oh, that name's here.
Korean Language and Literature.

534
00:46:38,567 --> 00:46:41,403
He and the girl from that record
were in the same major.

535
00:46:43,030 --> 00:46:44,489
I heard about this later,

536
00:46:44,573 --> 00:46:45,782
but that bastard

537
00:46:46,366 --> 00:46:47,868
wasn't even a university student.

538
00:46:48,410 --> 00:46:50,704
He was pretending to be one
from the start.

539
00:46:50,787 --> 00:46:51,747
Creepy, isn't it?

540
00:46:52,247 --> 00:46:54,416
It was just a regular vanity. Damn it.

541
00:46:54,499 --> 00:46:56,001
I said it first.

542
00:46:56,752 --> 00:46:58,879
Before I even asked him
what it looked like.

543
00:47:00,923 --> 00:47:02,174
Fuck.

544
00:47:25,322 --> 00:47:26,531
Yes, sir.

545
00:47:27,950 --> 00:47:29,451
I can't hear you. Say that again.

546
00:47:30,619 --> 00:47:31,828
We're following the trail.

547
00:47:32,663 --> 00:47:33,622
What? Who?

548
00:47:34,706 --> 00:47:37,542
Yeah, he came with us.
He said he wanted to help.

549
00:47:39,962 --> 00:47:40,796
Huh?

550
00:47:43,173 --> 00:47:44,007
Where did he go?

551
00:47:46,510 --> 00:47:47,719
Sir!

552
00:47:48,220 --> 00:47:49,680
Yeah? What is it?

553
00:47:51,515 --> 00:47:52,516
What is it?

554
00:47:54,476 --> 00:47:55,435
What?

555
00:47:55,519 --> 00:47:56,603
Here…

556
00:47:56,687 --> 00:47:58,230
Where's Je Moon-jae?

557
00:47:58,313 --> 00:47:59,606
Goddamn it.

558
00:48:00,273 --> 00:48:01,817
-Where is he?
-He's gone.

559
00:48:01,900 --> 00:48:04,027
-What?
-This is bullshit. Seriously.

560
00:48:19,459 --> 00:48:20,711
They won't find my uncle.

561
00:48:21,837 --> 00:48:25,674
He was buried somewhere on this mountain,
gone forever, just like Noja.

562
00:48:26,800 --> 00:48:30,137
I have to catch the Rat.
That's the only way.

563
00:48:31,596 --> 00:48:34,141
How am I supposed to prove I'm human?

564
00:48:34,683 --> 00:48:35,809
No.

565
00:48:35,892 --> 00:48:37,102
Even if I were the Rat,

566
00:48:37,853 --> 00:48:39,980
how could I ever admit it?

567
00:53:14,671 --> 00:53:17,590
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang

